  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25598398",
      "title": "Adding a re-usable \"Button\" Component",
      "sourceHash": "639387fc976025755ce11bd2ec913ea27ec1b72d396f0b1375d06491e4465748",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.14,
          "end": 4.03,
          "en": "So, time for a button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.03,
          "end": 8.07,
          "en": "Just like a card, a button is a default UI element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.07,
          "end": 8.903,
          "en": "which we're going to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.903,
          "end": 10.87,
          "en": "in different parts of the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.87,
          "end": 13.66,
          "en": "Therefore, here I'll add a Button.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.66,
          "end": 15.47,
          "en": "and I already mentioned it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.47,
          "end": 18.82,
          "en": "attached, you find a Button.Module.css file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.82,
          "end": 21.36,
          "en": "which I'll again download and drag and drop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.36,
          "end": 25.193,
          "en": "into that UI folder next to the Button.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.73,
          "end": 28.71,
          "en": "Now inside of the Button.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.71,
          "end": 30.36,
          "en": "we can import React from React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.36,
          "end": 32.69,
          "en": "because we're going to write some JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.69,
          "end": 34.1,
          "en": "We can import classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.1,
          "end": 39.1,
          "en": "from dot slash Button.Module.css already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.4,
          "end": 42.03,
          "en": "And we can then define our button constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.03,
          "end": 45.61,
          "en": "which is our functional component, and export,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.61,
          "end": 49.29,
          "en": "whoops, export this as a default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.29,
          "end": 51.58,
          "en": "And now in here, I simply want to return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.58,
          "end": 53.28,
          "en": "the built-in button component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.28,
          "end": 55.67,
          "en": "but of course, with my default styling applied",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.67,
          "end": 58.113,
          "en": "and with some configuration options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.95,
          "end": 60.29,
          "en": "To start with the styling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.29,
          "end": 64.57,
          "en": "I'll add class name and point at classes.button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.57,
          "end": 66.93,
          "en": "because in the Button.Module.css file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.93,
          "end": 68.8,
          "en": "you'll find that button class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 68.8,
          "end": 71.37,
          "en": "so we can use it thanks to CSS Modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 71.37,
          "end": 73.043,
          "en": "to apply a little styling here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.23,
          "end": 75.38,
          "en": "I also want to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 75.38,
          "end": 77.32,
          "en": "that the type of the button can be set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 77.32,
          "end": 80.38,
          "en": "and I want to make sure it can be set from outside,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 80.38,
          "end": 81.58,
          "en": "so from the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 81.58,
          "end": 84.5,
          "en": "where we use our accustomed button component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 84.5,
          "end": 87.03,
          "en": "They offer the value assigned to the type prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 87.03,
          "end": 89.96000000000001,
          "en": "on the built in button component will be dynamic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 89.96000000000001,
          "end": 94.21000000000001,
          "en": "and I will simply access props.type here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 94.21000000000001,
          "end": 95.97,
          "en": "but also provide a fallback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 95.97,
          "end": 99.45,
          "en": "in case that should not be set with the or operator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.45,
          "end": 101.303,
          "en": "The alternative is button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 102.16,
          "end": 104.15,
          "en": "So if props.type is undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 104.15,
          "end": 107.44,
          "en": "this button value will be used as a fallback type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 107.44,
          "end": 108.693,
          "en": "for the built in button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 110.03999999999999,
          "end": 112.21000000000001,
          "en": "Now, in addition, I'll add onClick,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 112.21000000000001,
          "end": 116.49000000000001,
          "en": "and here, I expect to get a handler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 116.49000000000001,
          "end": 118.92,
          "en": "via props on my own button component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 118.92,
          "end": 123.17,
          "en": "so I'll simply forward this to props onClick.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 123.17,
          "end": 125.38,
          "en": "Now that name here is totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 125.38,
          "end": 127.68,
          "en": "You don't have to name it onClick, but again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 127.68,
          "end": 130.67,
          "en": "I want to make my own button basically usable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 130.67,
          "end": 132.1,
          "en": "like the built in button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 132.1,
          "end": 134.59,
          "en": "and therefore I use the same naming.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 134.59,
          "end": 138.4,
          "en": "So I will have a onClick prop on my button component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 138.4,
          "end": 140.47,
          "en": "and any function received there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 140.47,
          "end": 143.32,
          "en": "is just passed onto the built in button component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 143.32,
          "end": 145.223,
          "en": "through its onClick prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 146.35,
          "end": 148.64,
          "en": "And last but not least here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 148.64,
          "end": 150.09,
          "en": "I also want to be able to output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 150.09,
          "end": 152.48,
          "en": "some content between the button tags,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 152.48,
          "end": 154.67000000000002,
          "en": "and I expect to get that content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 154.67000000000002,
          "end": 156.66,
          "en": "between the tags of my own button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 156.66,
          "end": 160.143,
          "en": "and therefore we use the special children prop here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 161.62,
          "end": 163.48,
          "en": "That should be all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 163.48,
          "end": 166.95,
          "en": "Now we can go to add user where we have a button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 166.95,
          "end": 169.34,
          "en": "and use our own custom button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 169.34,
          "end": 172.36,
          "en": "And hopefully I can now just replace built in button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 172.36,
          "end": 174.82,
          "en": "which is lowercase, with my custom button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 174.82,
          "end": 176.65,
          "en": "which starts with a capital B",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 176.65,
          "end": 178.98,
          "en": "per the convention that your components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 178.98,
          "end": 181.72,
          "en": "should always start with capital characters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 181.72,
          "end": 184.73,
          "en": "And we now just need to import it because as I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 184.73,
          "end": 186.77,
          "en": "you need to import all things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 186.77,
          "end": 188.63,
          "en": "you want to use from other files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 188.63,
          "end": 191.19,
          "en": "So here, I'll import button from,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 191.19,
          "end": 194.933,
          "en": "going up one level, UI Button like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 196.2,
          "end": 197.85,
          "en": "And if we now save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 197.85,
          "end": 199.41,
          "en": "we get this nice looking button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 199.41,
          "end": 201.87,
          "en": "which should work just like the built in button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 201.87,
          "end": 202.703,
          "en": "because in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 202.703,
          "end": 205.66,
          "en": "it just wraps the built in button, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 205.66,
          "end": 207.9,
          "en": "But that's the idea behind all React components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 207.9,
          "end": 209.64,
          "en": "In the end, you always compose them all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 209.64,
          "end": 211.91,
          "en": "from the building and HTML components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 211.91,
          "end": 213.66,
          "en": "but you structure them in a certain way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 213.66,
          "end": 215.45,
          "en": "and maybe attach certain logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 215.45,
          "end": 217.89,
          "en": "so that you have your own components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 217.89,
          "end": 220.06,
          "en": "And with that, that looks quite well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 220.06,
          "end": 222.88,
          "en": "Now let's make sure we actually fetch user input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 222.88,
          "end": 226.45,
          "en": "and we then kind of start rendering a list of users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 226.45,
          "end": 228.19299999999998,
          "en": "below that input form here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}